# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# dsh-codehub — never commit dependencies, credentials, or THROWAWAY build
# output. The list below is frozen by the project brief, with ONE deliberate
# exception, argued here so it is not "fixed" back:
#
#   `lib/` used to be ignored. That made the GitHub install path unusable:
#   DSH mounts this package as a git dependency (`github:yixing256/dsh-codehub`),
#   pnpm fetches the repository as-is and never builds it, so `main`/`exports`
#   (`lib/index.mjs`, `lib/client.js`) pointed at files that did not exist and
#   the loader reported `failed to import`. Every GitHub-installed DSH plugin
#   that does load (dsh-web-search-multi, dsh-plugin-console, …) commits its
#   `lib/` for exactly this reason. So the RUNTIME bundles are shipped in the
#   repository on purpose; only the transient intermediates stay ignored.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Dependencies and throwaway build output
node_modules/
dist/
coverage/

# Transient intermediates only. `pnpm run build` deletes client.cjs and
# client.css (the stylesheet is inlined into lib/client.js by
# scripts/wrap-client.mjs), so these rules exist to catch a half-finished build,
# never the shipped artifacts.
lib/client.cjs
lib/client.css
lib/**/*.map

# Logs
*.log

# Credentials and machine-local configuration — MUST NEVER BE COMMITTED
.env
.env.*
*.token
*.key
*.pem
credentials.json
user-config.local.json
*.local.yml
secrets.*

# Additional local-only files
*.local.json

# Editor / tooling scratch
*.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store

# Bundled dev scripts (scripts/smoke.ts is compiled here by `pnpm run smoke`)
scripts/.build/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Exceptions (added on purpose, do not remove).
# `.env.*` above would otherwise swallow the checked-in template, and the
# template is a shipped file (see package.json "files"). It carries empty
# placeholders only — never a real value.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!.env.example
